## Swift setup and pitfalls

The shared agents, hook adapters and unit loop are Python tools, so keep the
harness venv even though the application is Swift. The gate runs swift-format,
SwiftLint, build, tests and the shell ratchet. Resolve SwiftPM dependencies once
before entering a network-restricted agent session and commit Package.resolved.
{% if swift_build_system == 'xcode' %}

This scaffold does not generate an Xcode project. Keep your existing project or
workspace and shared scheme. `.harness/xcode.json` stores the container, scheme
and test destination as literal arguments. Add the examples/swift sources/tests
and the SnapshotTesting product (swift-snapshot-testing 1.18.7) to the appropriate
targets yourself; keep the accepted __Snapshots__ fixtures beside their tests.
Choose an installed simulator destination for iOS; platform=macOS is the default.
{% endif %}

- The CI runner is macos-15 with Xcode {{ xcode_version }} selected explicitly.
  Match that version and simulator OS before accepting UI image snapshots.
- Build output uses .build (Xcode DerivedData is .build/DerivedData). Compiler
  caches, SDKs and simulator services can still require sandbox access outside
  the checkout. Preflight the actual build/test commands; approve narrow access
  rather than disabling the sandbox. SwiftPM's manifest sandbox is another layer.
- macOS CI is more expensive than Linux. The workflow has a timeout; separate
  slow UI/device suites deliberately and consider appropriate path filters.
- withKnownIssue(isIntermittent: false) fails on an unexpected pass. Remove the
  wrapper once the pinned bug is fixed; do not make the known issue intermittent.
- Golden tests use swift-snapshot-testing with record: .never. A missing or
  changed fixture must fail without writing an accepted golden.
- NetworkStub blocks unknown requests only on sessions from makeSession(). Inject
  those sessions; URLSession.shared, sockets and WebSockets need separate guards.
  Deliberately classify loopback tests instead of assuming all tests are offline.
- SwiftLint --fix and swift-format edit the single supplied .swift file. The
  pre-commit hooks and check.sh check formatting without changing source files.
{% endif %}
